  "title": "Nephrectomy",
  "description": "Nephrectomy removes a kidney when it is affected by cancer, severe disease, chronic infection, or severe trauma. Your surgeon may use traditional open surgery or minimally invasive laparoscopic or robotic techniques. Modern surgical approaches have significantly reduced recovery time while maintaining excellent cancer outcomes. If you have two functional kidneys, loss of one is generally well-tolerated, and your remaining kidney typically maintains normal kidney function.",
